@anon.863986d00e4103fb69f29fe2b65b0919.814 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1790 x i8] }> <{ [1790 x i8] c"A cell in the table. Use this to position a cell manually or to apply\0Astyling. To do the latter, you can either use the function to override the\0Aproperties for a particular cell, or use it in show rules to apply certain\0Astyles to multiple cells at once.\0A\0APerhaps the most important use case of `{table.cell}` is to make a cell span\0Amultiple columns and/or rows with the `colspan` and `rowspan` fields.\0A\0A```example\0A>>> #set page(width: auto)\0A>>> #show table.cell.where(y: 0): strong\0A>>> #set table(\0A>>>   stroke: (x, y) => if y == 0 {\0A>>>     (bottom: 0.7pt + black)\0A>>>   },\0A>>>   align: (x, y) =>\0A>>>     if x > 0 { center }\0A>>>     else { left }\0A>>> )\0A#table(\0A  columns: 3,\0A  table.header(\0A    [Substance],\0A    [Subcritical \C2\B0C],\0A    [Supercritical \C2\B0C],\0A  ),\0A  [Hydrochloric Acid],\0A  [12.0], [92.1],\0A  [Sodium Myreth Sulfate],\0A  [16.6], [104],\0A  [Potassium Hydroxide],\0A  table.cell(colspan: 2)[24.7],\0A)\0A```\0A\0AFor example, you can override the fill, alignment or inset for a single\0Acell:\0A\0A```example\0A>>> #set page(width: auto)\0A// You can also import those.\0A#import table: cell, header\0A\0A#table(\0A  columns: 2,\0A  align: center,\0A  header(\0A    [*Trip progress*],\0A    [*Itinerary*],\0A  ),\0A  cell(\0A    align: right,\0A    fill: fuchsia.lighten(80%),\0A    [\F0\9F\9A\97],\0A  ),\0A  [Get in, folks!],\0A  [\F0\9F\9A\97], [Eat curbside hotdog],\0A  cell(align: left)[\F0\9F\8C\B4\F0\9F\9A\97],\0A  cell(\0A    inset: 0.06em,\0A    text(1.62em)[\F0\9F\9B\96\F0\9F\8C\85\F0\9F\8C\8A],\0A  ),\0A)\0A```\0A\0AYou may also apply a show rule on `table.cell` to style all cells at once.\0ACombined with selectors, this allows you to apply styles based on a cell's\0Aposition:\0A\0A```example\0A#show table.cell.where(x: 0): strong\0A\0A#table(\0A  columns: 3,\0A  gutter: 3pt,\0A  [Name], [Age], [Strength],\0A  [Hannes], [36], [Grace],\0A  [Irma], [50], [Resourcefulness],\0A  [Vikram], [49], [Perseverance],\0A)\0A```" }>, align 1
